        "math_academy_id": "q-161489",
        "problem": "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{y+1}\\frac{z}{4}\\,dz]dA\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 4x}.\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{y+1}\\frac{z}{4}\\,dz]dA & ={\u222c}_{D}{[\\frac{1}{8}{z}^{2}]}_{z=1}^{z=y+1}\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}\\frac{1}{8}((y+1)^{2}-1)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}\\frac{1}{8}({y}^{2}+2y)\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}\\frac{1}{8}({y}^{2}+2y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4x}\\frac{1}{8}({y}^{2}+2y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{4x}\\frac{1}{8}({y}^{2}+2y)\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{8}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}+{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=4x}dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}(64{x}^{3}-0)+(16{x}^{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{64}{3}{x}^{3}+16{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{[\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{4}+\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(1-0)+\\frac{2}{3}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
